 -bālī́, f. N. 🞄of a river (RV.¹).

vi-budha, a. very wise;
 m. god: 🞄-taṭinī, f. river of the gods, Ganges;
 -priya, 🞄a. dear to the wise or the gods;
 -rāja, m. 🞄king of the gods, Indra;
 -sadman, n. abode 🞄of the gods, heaven;
 -strī, f. celestial female;
 🞄-ācārya, m. instructor of the gods, Bṛhaspati;
 🞄-ādhipatya, n. sovereignty of the gods;
 🞄-anucara, m. attendant of a god;
 -āvāsa, 🞄m. dwelling of the gods, temple;
 -īśvara, 🞄m. lord of the gods.

vi-bodha, m. awaking;
 perceiving;
 🞄-bodhana, n. awaking (tr. & int.);
 -bodhayitavya, fp. to be awakened.
